1. DEFINITIONS

"Author" means Arkomiko (a creative pseudonym), the copyright holder of the Code.

"Code" means the source code of this repository: files in src/, .vscode/,
.github/ and configuration files in the repository root, excluding the
Author's Materials.

"Author's Materials" means everything listed in GiDo/RU-ru/NOTICE.md as not covered by
this license: the name and pseudonym Arkomiko, the logo, the mascot,
illustrations, favicons, placeholder covers, documentation graphics, music,
release artwork, texts and any other content in the contents_user/ folder.

"Own Project" means a website or page of an individual on which that
individual publishes their own works (music, artwork, video, texts) and
information about themselves, including when they sell their own works or
accept donations.

"Derivative Work" means the Code with modifications, as well as the Code or
parts of it included in other software.

2. PERMISSIONS

The Author grants a free, non-exclusive, worldwide license for the full term
of copyright to:

  a) study and run the Code;
  b) modify the Code and create Derivative Works;
  c) publish an Own Project based on the Code and Derivative Works;
  d) distribute the Code and Derivative Works free of charge, together with
     the source code and under this same license.

3. CONDITIONS

  a) All copies of the Code and Derivative Works must keep this LICENSE file
     and the GiDo/RU-ru/NOTICE.md file. The Author's copyright line must not be removed
     or changed; you may add your own copyright line below it.

  b) Every page of a published Own Project must show, in the footer, a visible
     credit linking to https://github.com/Arkomiko/Arkomiko.Music:
       in English: "Works on Astro and Vue. Built on the Arkomiko repo";
       in Russian: «Работает на Astro и Vue. Создано на основе репозитория Arkomiko».
     Size and styling are up to you, but the credit must be legible.

  c) All Author's Materials must be replaced with your own before an Own
     Project is published. See GiDo/RU-ru/NOTICE.md and GiDo/RU-ru/USAGE.md.

4. RESTRICTIONS

  a) You may not sell, rent, lease or sublicense the Code or Derivative Works,
     including as a template, theme, site builder or part of a paid product.
  b) You may not use the Code to provide paid services to others: building,
     configuring or maintaining websites to order, hosting, template marketplaces.
  c) You may not use the Code in projects of organizations (labels, studios,
     companies) without the Author's written permission.
  d) You may not use the Author's Materials except as permitted in GiDo/RU-ru/NOTICE.md.
  e) You may not present your Own Project as a project of Arkomiko or imply
     that it is affiliated with or endorsed by the Author.

5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Astro, Vue and other dependencies are distributed under the licenses of their
authors. This license does not apply to them and does not limit the rights
their licenses grant. It applies only to code written by the Author.

6. CONTRIBUTIONS

By submitting changes to the repository (a pull request), a contributor grants
the Author a non-exclusive, perpetual and irrevocable right to use, modify and
distribute the contribution under any terms, including this license.

7. TERMINATION

Your rights under this license terminate if you breach its conditions. If the
breach is cured within 30 days of notice from the Author, your rights are
reinstated.

8. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY AND LIABILITY

The Code is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied.
To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Author is not liable for any
damages arising in connection with the use of the Code.

9. MISCELLANEOUS

If any provision of this license is held invalid under applicable law, the
remaining provisions remain in effect. Rights beyond this license, including
commercial use of the Code, are granted only under a separate written
agreement. Contact: Arkomiko.Music@gmail.com.
